@startuml seq-pay-bill
title PayLink - Pay a Bill (ElectroCo) - Section 2.2, steps 1 to 8, plus Unknown re-query

' DECISIONS (see requirements.md, Ambiguities and decisions)
' - Participant names match the project folders. ElectroCoMock lives in /mocks (external to the monolith).
' - PayLink.Api is wiring only: it authenticates and forwards. PayLink.Payments orchestrates.
' - Inquiry failures (missing field, bill not found, biller timeout) return an error:
'   no payment, no hold, no ledger entry.
' - Pay order: idempotency check, biller/service active check, min/max validation (bill amount only),
'   then the payment is created. A refusal before creation creates nothing.
' - Idempotency record stores a fingerprint of the request data. A concurrent insert that hits the
'   unique key is treated as "in progress".
' - Daily limit, velocity and blocked account are rules in PayLink.Fraud and give Rejected.
' - PayLink.Accounts writes each ledger entry and its audit record in ONE transaction (FR-25).
' - PayLink.Notifications is asynchronous (in-process event): a failure never changes the payment.
' - Failed -> Refunded (hold released once) is defined only in seq-refund-failed.
' - TopUpNet callbacks (hard case 6) are a separate flow, not shown here: the payment waits in
'   SentToBiller and the callback is handled by PayLink.BillerIntegration and PayLink.Payments (US-18).

actor Scheduler
participant CustomerApp
participant "PayLink.Api" as Api
participant "PayLink.Payments" as Payments
participant "PayLink.Catalog" as Catalog
participant "PayLink.Fraud" as Fraud
participant "PayLink.Fees" as Fees
participant "PayLink.Accounts" as Accounts
participant "PayLink.BillerIntegration" as BillerIntegration
participant ElectroCoMock
participant "PayLink.Notifications" as Notifications

== Step 1: Login and limits ==
CustomerApp -> Api : login(credentials)
Api -> Accounts : authenticate + getVerificationLevel(customerId)
Accounts --> Api : verificationLevel
Api --> CustomerApp : session established

== Steps 2 and 3: Bill inquiry, fee and total (creates no payment, no hold, no ledger entry) ==
CustomerApp -> Api : inquireBill(billerServiceId, inputFields)
Api -> Payments : inquire(billerServiceId, inputFields)
Payments -> Catalog : getService(billerServiceId)
Catalog --> Payments : service (active?, required fields)
alt Biller or service not found or disabled
    Payments --> Api : error(biller unavailable)
    Api --> CustomerApp : error(biller unavailable)
else Biller active
    alt A required field is missing (e.g. meterNumber)
        Payments --> Api : error(missing field: meterNumber)
        Api --> CustomerApp : error(missing field), no amounts shown
    else All required fields present
        Payments -> BillerIntegration : inquire(ElectroCo, meterNumber)
        BillerIntegration -> ElectroCoMock : GET bill(meterNumber)
        alt Biller has no bill for this meter number
            ElectroCoMock --> BillerIntegration : not found
            BillerIntegration --> Payments : billNotFound
            Payments --> Api : error(bill not found)
            Api --> CustomerApp : error(bill not found), no amounts shown
        else No answer within 10 seconds
            BillerIntegration --> Payments : timeout
            Payments --> Api : error(try again later)
            Api --> CustomerApp : error(try again later), no amounts shown
        else Bill found
            ElectroCoMock --> BillerIntegration : amountDue = 350.00 EGP
            BillerIntegration --> Payments : bill(350.00 EGP)
            Payments -> Fees : calculateFee(ElectroCo, 350.00)
            Fees --> Payments : fee = 2.50 EGP
            Payments --> Api : quote: amount 350.00 + fee 2.50 = total 352.50 EGP
            Api --> CustomerApp : quote: amount 350.00 + fee 2.50 = total 352.50 EGP
        end
    end
end

== Pay ==
CustomerApp -> Api : pay(quoteId, idempotencyKey)
Api -> Payments : pay(customerId, quoteId, idempotencyKey)
Payments -> Payments : look up idempotencyKey + compare request fingerprint
alt Key used with DIFFERENT request data
    Payments --> Api : error(idempotency key reused with different data), nothing created
    Api --> CustomerApp : error
else Key used, first request still in progress
    Payments --> Api : in progress status, nothing created
    Api --> CustomerApp : in progress
else Key used, first request already finished (any state)
    Payments --> Api : original payment result (no new payment, charge or hold)
    Api --> CustomerApp : original result
else New key
    note over Payments, Catalog : Re-check before the payment exists
    Payments -> Catalog : isActive(billerServiceId) + getLimits(billerServiceId)
    Catalog --> Payments : active?, min 5.00 / max 10,000.00 EGP
    alt Biller or service disabled since the inquiry
        Payments --> Api : error(biller disabled), no payment, no hold
        Api --> CustomerApp : error(biller disabled)
    else Bill amount below 5.00 or above 10,000.00 EGP
        Payments --> Api : error(below minimum / above maximum), no payment, no hold
        Api --> CustomerApp : error(reason)
    else Biller active and amount within limits
        Payments -> Payments : create payment [Initiated]\nstore idempotencyKey (unique index) with fingerprint

        note over Payments, Fraud : Step 4: Fraud checks (chain: daily limit, velocity, blocked account)
        Payments -> Fraud : check(customerId, amount 350.00, verificationLevel)
        alt Velocity rule fails (more than 5 payments in 60 s)
            Fraud -> Accounts : blockAccount(customerId, 10 minutes, reason = "velocity")
            Accounts --> Fraud : blocked (block + audit record)
            Fraud --> Payments : rejected(reason)
            Payments -> Payments : transition Initiated -> Rejected
            Payments --> Api : payment [Rejected] + reason
            Api --> CustomerApp : rejected(reason)
        else Daily limit exceeded or account blocked
            Fraud --> Payments : rejected(reason)
            Payments -> Payments : transition Initiated -> Rejected
            Payments --> Api : payment [Rejected] + reason
            Api --> CustomerApp : rejected(reason)
        else All rules pass
            Fraud --> Payments : passed

            note over Payments, Accounts : Step 5: Hold the money
            Payments -> Accounts : placeHold(walletId, 352.50 EGP, paymentId)
            note right of Accounts : Ledger entries + audit records\nwritten in ONE transaction
            alt Insufficient funds (hard case 4)
                Accounts --> Payments : insufficientFunds
                Payments -> Payments : transition Initiated -> Rejected
                Payments --> Api : payment [Rejected] + reason
                Api --> CustomerApp : rejected(insufficient funds)
            else Funds available
                Accounts --> Payments : holdPlaced(holdId)
                Payments -> Payments : transition Initiated -> FundsHeld

                note over Payments, ElectroCoMock : Step 6: Call the biller
                Payments -> Payments : transition FundsHeld -> SentToBiller
                Payments -> BillerIntegration : pay(reference = paymentId, 350.00 EGP)
                BillerIntegration -> ElectroCoMock : POST payment(reference, 350.00)

                note over Payments, ElectroCoMock : Step 7: Confirmation
                alt Biller confirms (paid)
                    ElectroCoMock --> BillerIntegration : paid
                    BillerIntegration --> Payments : confirmed
                    Payments -> Accounts : completeHold(holdId, feeIncome 2.50, agentCommission 1.00 if agent)
                    note right of Accounts : ONE transaction: hold -> final charge,\nfee income, agent commission (40% of fee,\nPayLink keeps 1.50), ledger entries + audit records
                    Accounts --> Payments : charged
                    Payments -> Payments : transition SentToBiller -> Completed

                    note over Payments, Notifications : Step 8: Receipt (asynchronous)
                    Payments ->> Notifications : PaymentCompleted event\n(SMS + push)
                    Payments --> Api : payment [Completed]
                    Api --> CustomerApp : receipt
                else Biller refuses (error code)
                    ElectroCoMock --> BillerIntegration : refused(errorCode)
                    BillerIntegration --> Payments : refused(errorCode)
                    Payments -> Payments : transition SentToBiller -> Failed
                    ref over Payments, Accounts, Notifications : seq-refund-failed\n(release hold once, Failed -> Refunded, notify)
                    Payments --> Api : payment [Refunded] + reason
                    Api --> CustomerApp : failed(reason), money returned
                else No answer within 10 seconds (hard case 2)
                    BillerIntegration --> Payments : timeout
                    Payments -> Payments : transition SentToBiller -> Unknown
                    note right of Accounts : Hold stays active.\nNo refund while Unknown.
                    Payments ->> Notifications : PaymentProcessing event
                    Payments --> Api : payment [Unknown]
                    Api --> CustomerApp : payment is being processed
                end
            end
        end
    end
end

== Unknown re-query (background, no customer request) ==
note over Scheduler, Payments : Re-query times are cumulative from the moment the payment became Unknown.
loop up to 3 times (after 1, 5 and 15 minutes)
    Scheduler ->> Payments : requeueUnknown(paymentId)
    Payments -> BillerIntegration : queryStatus(reference = paymentId)
    BillerIntegration -> ElectroCoMock : GET payment(reference)
    alt Biller confirms (paid)
        ElectroCoMock --> BillerIntegration : paid
        BillerIntegration --> Payments : confirmed
        Payments -> Accounts : completeHold(holdId, feeIncome 2.50, agentCommission 1.00 if agent)
        Accounts --> Payments : charged
        Payments -> Payments : transition Unknown -> Completed
        Payments ->> Notifications : PaymentCompleted event\n(SMS + push)
        note over Scheduler, Payments : Stop re-querying.
    else Biller refuses, or has no such payment
        ElectroCoMock --> BillerIntegration : refused / not found
        BillerIntegration --> Payments : refused
        Payments -> Payments : transition Unknown -> Failed
        ref over Payments, Accounts, Notifications : seq-refund-failed\n(release hold once, Failed -> Refunded, notify)
        note over Scheduler, Payments : Stop re-querying.
    else No answer
        BillerIntegration --> Payments : timeout
        note right of Payments : Stays Unknown. Hold stays active.\nNo refund.
    end
end
note over Payments, Accounts : After the 3rd unanswered re-query the payment stays Unknown with the hold kept.\nThe reconciliation job (US-32) resolves it later with the same transitions:\nUnknown -> Completed, or Unknown -> Failed then seq-refund-failed.
@enduml